SEG = "STO"
CAT = "fvicStorage"
Q = [
    ("Under Schedule 4 as it now stands, a category A or B longarm must be stored in a:",
     "Purpose-built steel safe", ["Hard wood wardrobe", "Locked glass cabinet", "Locked garden tool shed"],
     "Schedule 4 item 1(1), as substituted in 2021, requires a purpose-built steel storage receptacle. Older guides still mention hard wood, but the current Act says steel."),
    ("The steel of a category A or B gun safe must be at least how thick under Schedule 4?",
     "1.6 mm", ["0.8 mm", "3.0 mm", "6.0 mm"],
     "Schedule 4 item 1(1)(a) requires steel at least 1.6 mm thick that complies with Australian/New Zealand Standard 1594:2002."),
    ("Your empty gun safe weighs 80 kg. Under Schedule 4 it must be:",
     "Bolted to the building", ["Fitted with an intruder alarm", "Kept out of sight", "Kept in a locked room"],
     "Schedule 4 item 1(1)(b) requires a receptacle weighing less than 150 kg when empty to be bolted to the structure of the premises where the firearm is kept."),
    ("Above how many firearms on the premises must an intruder alarm be fitted under Schedule 4?",
     "15", ["5", "10", "25"],
     "Schedule 4 item 1(2) requires an intruder alarm system when more than 15 firearms are stored on the premises."),
    ("An intruder alarm required by Schedule 4 must, when triggered, activate an audible alarm and:",
     "A visible outside light", ["A message to police", "A siren inside only", "A camera recording"],
     "Schedule 4 item 1(2)(b) requires the alarm to activate an audible alarm warning device and an external visible alarm warning light, and to meet AS 2201.1:2007."),
    ("Under Schedule 4, ammunition for a category A or B longarm must be stored:",
     "In its own locked container", ["In the safe beside the rifle", "In the rifle's magazine", "Locked in the glove box"],
     "Schedule 4 item 1(3) requires cartridge ammunition to be stored in a locked container separate from the receptacle in which the firearm is stored."),
    ("For category C or D firearms, Schedule 4 says the safe's key must be carried by the holder or:",
     "Kept securely in another room", ["Hung on a hook beside the safe", "Kept in the same room as the safe", "Kept with the ammunition"],
     "Schedule 4 item 2(2A) requires the key to be carried by the licence holder or kept securely in a separate room from the receptacle when it is not being accessed."),
    ("When does s 121 require a category A or B longarm to be in its approved storage?",
     "Whenever not carried or used", ["Only overnight at home", "Only when you go away", "Only during closed season"],
     "Section 121(1) requires storage in the Schedule 4 manner whenever the firearm is not being carried or used."),
    ("Beyond the Schedule 4 minimum, the Firearm Safety Code booklet encourages a safe with:",
     "Separate access for ammunition", ["A two-key lock", "Room for ammunition inside", "A fireproof lining"],
     "The booklet recommends a commercial, purpose-built safe and encourages separate access points for firearms and ammunition."),
    ("The Firearm Safety Code booklet advises against storing firearms in:",
     "Old school lockers", ["Bolted steel safes", "Purpose-built cabinets", "Commercial gun safes"],
     "The booklet recommends a commercial standard, purpose-built safe and says not to use old school lockers, which can be easily penetrated."),
    ("Firearms are being kept in an empty house after the owner's death. The booklet recommends:",
     "Moving them to a lived-in home", ["Leaving them locked there", "Handing them to the executor", "Taking them to a club"],
     "The booklet says that if firearms are stored in an empty house, they should be relocated and stored in an occupied residence."),
    ("Family members are worried about a licence holder's mental health. Victoria Police says a common step is to:",
     "Store them at another address", ["Hand the licence in to police", "Hide the ammunition", "Change the safe code"],
     "The booklet says that where health issues are identified, a common recommendation is to move the firearms to a storage address other than the holder's home."),
    ("The booklet says children who find a firearm should be taught to:",
     "Get help from an adult", ["Unload it carefully", "Put it back where it was", "Carry it to an adult"],
     "The booklet says children should be taught not to touch a firearm without an adult present and, if they find one, to seek the help of an adult."),
    ("The booklet says a padded cover or hard case for travel helps because it protects the firearm and:",
     "Is less likely to alarm people", ["Lets you carry it loaded", "Takes the place of a safe", "Counts as approved storage"],
     "The booklet advises a padded cover or hard case, which protects the firearm and makes it less obvious, so it is less likely to alarm members of the public."),
    ("The course slides say that in a vehicle your firearm should be stored out of sight, preferably in:",
     "A lockable gun case", ["The locked glove box", "The back seat pocket", "Under a floor mat"],
     "The slides say to store the firearm out of sight, preferably in a lockable gun case, unloaded, with ammunition in a separate container."),
    ("When away camping with firearms, the booklet suggests not having which on your car?",
     "Firearm stickers", ["Tinted windows", "A locked canopy", "A long-range antenna"],
     "The booklet says firearm stickers on a car only alert others to firearms that may be stored in the vehicle."),
    ("The booklet's tips for storing firearms at a campsite include keeping the bolts:",
     "Out and stored apart", ["In the rifles, locked", "With the ammunition", "In the car's glove box"],
     "The booklet's tips for safe storage away from home include storing firearms out of sight, ammunition separately in a locked box, and bolts removed and stored separately."),
    ("According to the booklet, you should have unloaded firearms in your vehicle only when:",
     "Travelling for a genuine reason", ["The car is locked", "The firearm is in a hard case", "It is daylight"],
     "The booklet says you need a lawful, proper and sufficient purpose, so firearms should be in a vehicle only on the way to or from a hunt, a range or another genuine reason."),
    ("You need to take a firearm on a train or plane. The booklet says to:",
     "Plan it with the carrier first", ["Wrap it in a blanket in your bag", "Take only the bolt", "Tell other passengers"],
     "The booklet says public transport of firearms can alarm passengers and to make suitable arrangements, including discussing transport requirements with your travel agent or the carrier."),
    ("The booklet says that when you get back home or to camp after shooting, you should lock away the firearm and ammunition:",
     "Straight away, separately", ["Within 24 hours", "After cleaning it", "Together in one safe"],
     "Rule 6 in the booklet says to lock away your unloaded firearm and ammunition separately, immediately when you return to camp or home."),
]
